Third-party data and notes
- ecoinvent. The life-cycle impact assessment uses the ecoinvent database v3.7 (cut-off system model; ecoinvent
  Association). No ecoinvent data are included in this repository: neither the characterisation factors (TRACI 2.1
  scores) of the ecoinvent datasets nor any result file from which they could be recalculated. The factor template
  (01_Data/03_Reference/LCA-FCDI_D01_Reference_TRACIFactorsTemplate_v01.csv) and the flow dictionary
  (01_Data/03_Reference/LCA-FCDI_D01_Reference_FlowDictionary_v01.csv) name the ecoinvent datasets used (activity, reference
  product, location, reference unit) and carry no values; the dummy table
  (01_Data/03_Reference/LCA-FCDI_D01_Reference_TRACIFactorsDummy_v01.csv) carries 1.0 for every factor. Users with an ecoinvent
  licence supply the factors themselves. Credit: Wernet, G., Bauer, C., Steubing, B., Reinhard, J., Moreno-Ruiz, E.
  and Weidema, B. (2016). The ecoinvent database version 3 (part I): overview and methodology. Int. J. Life Cycle
  Assess. 21, 1218-1230.
- TRACI. The impact categories and the US 2008 per-capita normalisation factors are those of TRACI 2.1 (U.S.
  Environmental Protection Agency); the normalisation factors were transcribed from the authors' workbook.
- Literature, vendor and measured values. Values taken from published sources, vendor catalogues and quotations are
  cited in the source and reference columns of the CSV files (for example the benchmark treatment costs); please
  cite those sources as well when you reuse the values. The electron partitioning (D05) was measured in the
  41-day continuous campaign of Riveros et al., Water Res. 2026, 303, 126244, with the reactor of Riveros et al.,
  Water Res. 2025, 271, 122844.
- Consumer price index. The CPI-U annual averages (U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, series CUUR0000SA0) are public
  data of the U.S. government.
